        <h2>What is GCD?</h2>

        <p>
            GCD stands for Greatest Common Divisor. It is the largest
            positive number that divides two numbers without leaving
            a remainder.
        </p>

        <p>
            For example, the GCD of 12 and 18 is 6.
        </p>


        <h2>What is LCM?</h2>

        <p>
            LCM stands for Least Common Multiple. It is the smallest
            positive number that is a multiple of both numbers.
        </p>

        <p>
            For example, the LCM of 12 and 18 is 36.
        </p>


